  "result": "Perfect! All 181 tests pass. I've successfully created a customer statements module:\n\n**`src/statements.js` provides:**\n\n**`statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)`** \u2014 Generates a customer statement\n- **Input:**\n  - `customerId`: Customer identifier (normalized internally)\n  - `invoices`: Array of all invoices to filter\n  - `asOf`: Cutoff date in YYYY-MM-DD format\n\n- **Filtering logic:**\n  - Only invoices for the specified customer\n  - Only invoices with status `'issued'` or `'partially_paid'`\n  - Only invoices with `issueDate` on or before `asOf`\n\n- **Returns:** `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })`\n  - `customerId`: Normalized customer ID\n  - `invoices`: Array of statement line items sorted by issueDate ascending\n  - Each invoice includes:\n    - `number`: Invoice number\n    - `issueDate`: Issue date\n    - `dueDate`: Due date\n    - `total`: Invoice total amount (after all adjustments)\n    - `due`: Amount still owed (from `balanceDue`)\n  - `totalDue`: Sum of all due amounts\n\n- **Errors:**\n  - `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND`: Unknown or invalid customer ID\n\n**Test coverage includes:**\n- Customer and status filtering\n- Date filtering (before, equal to, after cutoff)\n- Handling draft and paid invoices\n- Partial payments affecting due amounts\n- Sorting and totals calculation\n- Normalized customer IDs\n- Empty statement handling\n\nCustomer statements are now ready for generating aged receivables reports and collection tracking. \u2714",
